<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="033" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>DataGrid Money columns sort by value + Export writes formatted values (FR-20, #2446, #2447)</title>
    <phase>3 Grids, information, messages</phase>
    <gate>after 028 and 032</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies the shared DataGrid sort and CSV export (.ts/.tsx) used by many surfaces</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Two scoped fixes in named functions with a clear expected result</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>D</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>028, 032</deps>
    <tags>frontend, typescript, unit-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>In the shared DataGrid, make Money (currency) columns sort by numeric value, and make CSV Export write the same text the Money cell displays.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. TypeScript developer on the shared DataGrid.</role>
  <goal>Sorting $9 / $10 / $100 orders them by value in both directions, and an exported Money cell's text equals the displayed value; every other column type sorts and exports as before.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-20; design §7 (the invoice grid shows two Money columns since R3 task 002: `sprk_totalamount`, `sprk_totalamount_base`). Sort: the column comparator (`DataGrid.tsx:1160-1175`) compares numerically only when both raw values are JS numbers; otherwise it compares the displayed strings (`renderCellValue` + `formattedLabelOf`), so a Money value that arrives as a non-number, or as a number with a formatted label, sorts as text ("$10" before "$9"). Find which shape the external module fetch actually returns for Money (raw number, string, object, `@formattedValues` label) before choosing the fix; cite it in the notes. Display: `renderCellValue` 'currency' branch (`DataGrid.tsx:622-640`) and `usesFormattedLabel` (`:606-611`). Export: `exportCsv` writes raw `record[c.name]` (`commandBar/csvExport.ts:150-178`, line `:167`) — so Money exports unformatted. The existing export test is `commandBar/__tests__/csvExport.test.ts`.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/DataGrid.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/commandBar/csvExport.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/commandBar/CommandBar.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/commandBar/__tests__/csvExport.test.ts</file>
      <file role="new-artifact">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/__tests__/DataGrid.moneySort.test.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/__tests__/DataGrid.formattedValues.test.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="028" status="pending">P2 deployed (phase-deploy convention)</dependency>
      <dependency task="032" status="pending">DataGrid.tsx changes for persisted settings land first (same file)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec FR-20">Money columns (renderer 'currency', or a money attribute type as the resolver derives it) sort by numeric value in both directions; null/empty sort as today's empties do (state the rule in the notes and test it).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec FR-20">For Money columns, the exported cell text equals the cell's displayed text (same `renderCellValue` + formatted-label path). Export for every other renderer is unchanged in this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">No change to `DataGridProps`, the CSV filename, BOM, CRLF or quoting rules; other consumers' behaviour for non-Money columns is unchanged (tests stay green).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Coordinate the change with the dataset-grid framework owners (the same contact as 032); record their OK in the notes.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/spec.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/SPAARKE-DATAGRID-FRAMEWORK-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/fluent-v9-component/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-component-authoring.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/ui-test/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Display string as sort key" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/DataGrid.tsx">task 061 comparator — extend it with a Money branch, do not replace it</pattern>
      <pattern name="Export unit tests" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/commandBar/__tests__/csvExport.test.ts">pure-function tests for exportCsv</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load the knowledge files, read the relevant files, declare rigor and model tier per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">Establish the Money value shape the grid receives (mock and, if needed, the BFF module fetch code); write it in the notes.</step>
    <step order="2">Extract the comparator into a testable function; add a Money branch that compares numeric value.</step>
    <step order="3">Make export use the display text for Money columns (pass the formatted-label lookup into `exportCsv` or pre-render at the CommandBar call site).</step>
    <step order="4">Tests: $9/$10/$100 ascending and descending; nulls; a non-Money number column and a text column sort as before; Money export text equals `renderCellValue` output; non-Money export unchanged.</step>
    <step order="5">Run the shared-lib DataGrid tests and the SPA build.</step>
    <step order="6">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` and this POML's &lt;status&gt; to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="7">Record deviations and the value-shape finding in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-033-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the framework owners want formatted export for every column type (not only Money), STOP and ask the owner: that changes every consumer's CSV and is beyond FR-20 as written.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Money sort and export">
      <url>https://{spa-dev-host}/</url>
      <steps>
        <step>On the Invoices tab sort by Total amount ascending and descending</step>
        <step>Export to CSV; open it</step>
        <step>Compare an exported Total amount with the cell on screen</step>
        <step>Check the console for errors</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Value order; exported text equals the displayed text</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps><step>Switch to dark mode on the Invoices grid</step></steps>
      <expected>No visual change from this task; semantic tokens only</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Run shared-lib tests and the SPA build</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/DataGrid.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/commandBar/csvExport.ts</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/__tests__/DataGrid.moneySort.test.ts</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/commandBar/__tests__/csvExport.test.ts</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-033-notes.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A Money column with $9, $10 and $100 sorts 9, 10, 100 ascending and 100, 10, 9 descending.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Empty Money values sort by the rule recorded in the notes, consistently in both directions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An exported Money cell's text equals the displayed cell text.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Non-Money columns sort and export exactly as before; existing DataGrid and csvExport tests pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `DataGridProps` change; filename, BOM, CRLF and quoting unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The framework owners' OK is recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-20; issues #2446 (sort), #2447 (export).</notes>

